# Intramolecular ring closure / opening on a single molecule —
# A(x,y) <-> A(x!1,y!1).  Partial-scaling validation for the Phase-3
# *unimolecular intramolecular ring closure* (single-molecule AddBond, x bonded
# to y on the SAME molecule) and *ring opening* (single-molecule DeleteBond that
# keeps the molecule, n_product_patterns == 1) batch-fire paths.
#
#     A(x,y)       ->^kclose  A(x!1,y!1)   (intramolecular self-bond, AddBond)
#     A(x!1,y!1)   ->^kopen   A(x,y)       (ring opening, DeleteBond)
#
# This is a two-state first-order reversible system (open monomer <-> closed
# monomer); every molecule is its own singleton complex, so the K batched
# firings are molecule-disjoint with NO same-complex interaction — the cleanest
# possible intramolecular test.  Well-mixed mass action:
#     d[closed]/dt = kclose*[open] - kopen*[closed] = 0
#       =>  [closed]/[open] = kclose/kopen.
# With kclose = kopen = 1 and A_tot = 1000 the equilibrium is
# [open] = [closed] = 500.  The seed sits at that equilibrium, so the ensemble
# is stationary from t = 0 and any first-moment bias in either scaled batch path
# (the AddBond ring closure or the DeleteBond ring opening) shows up as a drift
# of the observable mean.
#
# Minimum reactant population at equilibrium = 500 (open A for the closure /
# closed A for the opening), so a critical size Nc gives K = floor(500/Nc):
# Nc=50 -> K=10, Nc=100 -> K=5, Nc=200 -> K=2 — real batching with an analytic
# first moment of exactly 500.
#
# Oracle for the scaled (Nc > 0) path: the analytic equilibrium (500/500), the
# exact-RM ensemble, and BNG2 (ODE/SSA).  NFsim has no partial scaling and is
# NOT an oracle for it.

begin parameters
    kclose     1.0
    kopen      1.0
    Aopen_ss   500      # open monomers at equilibrium
    Aclosed_ss 500      # closed (self-looped) monomers at equilibrium
end parameters

begin molecule types
    A(x,y)
end molecule types

begin seed species
    A(x,y)        Aopen_ss
    A(x!1,y!1)    Aclosed_ss
end seed species

begin observables
    Molecules  Aopen    A(x,y)
    Molecules  Aclosed  A(x!1,y!1)
end observables

begin reaction rules
    close:  A(x,y)     -> A(x!1,y!1)  kclose
    open:   A(x!1,y!1) -> A(x,y)      kopen
end reaction rules

begin actions
    simulate({method=>"nf",t_end=>10,n_steps=>100})
end actions
